  hi let me call you right back i'm doing  a scene  that wasn't the only cellular mishap on  the series though aniston was also the  recipient of another unexpected dial-in  while taping her birthday scene on the  set of the one where they all turned 30  which just goes to show that she was as  widely reported very popular during her  time on the show better to be over the  hill  this gate comes with a phone  sometimes a blooper isn't an accident  sometimes it's a prank in the one with  the secret closet joey has to take a  pregnant rachel to the hospital after  she begins experiencing braxton hicks  contractions ross shows up late  complaining about the distance between  himself and his baby's mother to be  schwimmer had a hard time hitting his  cues for the scene though so matt  leblanc and jennifer aniston decided to  pull a prank on him after schwimmer  missed his mark and had to go back out  of frame to try again the two decided to  hide and let him walk into an empty room  just to see what he'd do  later when he forgot his line during a  take aniston playfully laid into him for  bringing the whole gang down and at the  the movie theater guys just suck  what happened here you used to be able  to act i know  remember joey's disastrous noodle soup  commercial audition with the kid who was  a more competent actor than him  um soup  i mean noodle soup i mean soup  well life imitated art in that regard  because cole sprouse who portrayed ben  in the later seasons of the show seemed  to be the only one who'd memorized the  script while shooting a scene with  jennifer aniston for the one with the  truth about london for example sprouse  confidently fed her the missing line  when she forgot what to say  now what is my first line  why did we agree okay  then when he shared the screen with  david schwimmer for a scene in the one  with the holiday armadillo sprouse had  to again remind his co-star of what to  say next  oh  chandler and monica's storyline in the  one where ross meets elizabeth's dad is  kind of a throwaway the two have a silly  misunderstanding over what time they're  supposed to meet up for a mini date and  their snafu becomes spotter for phoebe's  next book chapter their argument doesn't  make many friends fans lists of best  moments of course but perhaps it would  have if it had gone down the way it did  in the bloopers  we said we would meet at the coffee  house at six we said seven you dumb egg  of all the cast members who were paired  for two-person scenes throughout friends  lisa kudrow and david schwimmer had to  be among the most entertaining phoebe is  never afraid to call ross on his worst  decisions and since she seems to be the  one woman in his life who is neither a  relative nor an ex she's often his go-to  friend for unbiased advice the two also  get into a lot of weird situations  together including the time that they  each date half of a divorcing couple and  start bickering with each other in the  one with the engagement picture as their  arguments started to mimic the separated  couple david schwimmer and lisa kudrow  had a lot of trouble keeping it together  and finishing their scenes  and she uses sex as a weapon fine  things got so out of hand that schwimmer  suggested shooting the scene line by  line which kudrow seemed to game for  apparently it had worked out pretty well  for her before we'll just do the same  one line at a time  yeah one a legion i got an emmy  as friends joey and chandler definitely  find comfort in each other they're known  to hug so often that they eventually  have to ask themselves if it's getting  out of hand in the season 6 episode the  one with the mac and cheese during  shooting all of the repeated hugs and  back rubs started to get under their  skin  while we're here anything else  get off me  then things really went off the rails  when the mats decided to lean into the  discomfort of prolonged physical contact  what's that in your pocket  after so many seasons of 